# Motion and animation

## Layers
1. Tokens: lib/core/motion/motion_tokens.dart is the only file with Duration and Curve values used for motion.
2. Policy: MotionPolicy resolves MotionTier (full, reduced, minimal) from MediaQuery.disableAnimations, the FrameBudgetMonitor (profile/release only; downgrades after sustained jank, never upgrades mid-session) and the app lifecycle (ambient motion pauses in background).
3. Profile: MotionProfile exposes scaleDuration, allowsAmbient, allowsDepthEffects, maxStaggerItems and animatesEntrances. Read it with context.motion.
4. Primitives in lib/core/motion/primitives, painters in lib/core/motion/painters, transitions in lib/core/motion/transitions.
5. Orchestration: a screen with staggered motion owns one AnimationController and derives Intervals from StaggerSchedule.

## Hard rules
- Durations and curves come only from MotionTokens. Scale every duration with the profile.
- Create controllers in initState and dispose them. Never create a controller in build. Never one controller per list item.
- Never call setState on every tick. Use AnimatedBuilder with a child or transition widgets.
- Animate only transform and opacity (FadeTransition, SlideTransition, ScaleTransition, Transform). No Opacity on large subtrees, no animated blur, BackdropFilter, saveLayer-heavy clips or animated shadows.
- At most two ambient animations visible at once. Entrance animations run once per route entry, never on rebuild.
- Inactive tabs and routes stop their tickers (TickerMode in the shell).
- Shimmer uses one controller per SkeletonScope and one ShaderMask per SkeletonGroup.
- Painters take repaint: animation, implement a precise shouldRepaint, allocate nothing in paint and sit inside a RepaintBoundary.
- Multiply travel distances and amplitudes by LayoutMetrics.motionScale.
- Every primitive has a minimal-tier path that skips or shortens to a fade, and a widget test covering it.
- Lottie, Rive, 3D engines and fragment shaders need an ADR with a size budget, lazy loading, tier gating and a static fallback.

## Primitive catalog
- StaggeredEntrance and StaggerSchedule: one controller, Interval slots, capped by maxStaggerItems.
- FadeSlideIn: one-shot fade plus slide.
- PressableScale: press feedback by scale.
- ShakeOnTrigger: horizontal shake when a trigger value changes.
- CountUpText: integer count-up with a formatter.
- AnimatedQuantityText: vertical roll when a number changes.
- PopIn: overshoot scale entrance.
- PulseAttention: ambient pulse, disabled when ambient motion is not allowed.
- SlidingPillIndicator: pill that slides between equal-width slots.
- MotionTransitions: sharedAxisHorizontal, fadeThrough and fadeScale route builders, used by lib/config/routes/route_transitions.dart.
- FadeThroughTabStack: keeps shell tabs alive, fades through on switch and mutes inactive tickers.
- HeroTags: the only source of Hero tags.
- PerspectiveTilt: drag-driven Matrix4 perspective tilt with spring-back.
- AutoPlayCarouselController: timer-driven PageController that pauses on interaction and when ambient motion is off.
- MorphingProgressRing: steps through 25, 50, 75 and 100 percent and morphs into a check.
- Painters: ArcSweepPainter and CheckMorphPainter.

## Budgets
- docs/PERFORMANCE_BUDGET.md defines frame, asset and size budgets enforced by tool/check_asset_budget.dart. docs/ANIMATION_GUIDE.md holds the profile-mode checklist.
